### 2. Server-Side RBAC Enforcement (June 14, 2026)

**What changed:**
- `src/app/api/admin/checkins/route.ts` — added centralized `ACTION_PERMISSIONS` map gating all 45 actions; removed 17 inline `role !== "admin"` checks; `update` relaxed from admin-only to `canEditRecords`; `delete` relaxed to `canDeleteRecords`; `deleteBooking` relaxed to `canDeleteBooking`; `getSetting` restricted to admin-only
- `src/app/api/admin/food-orders/route.ts` — `authenticateUser` upgraded to return permissions; 20 actions gated (view=`canViewFoodOrders`, payment=`canMarkPaid`, cleanup=admin-only)
- `src/app/api/admin/expenses/route.ts` — `authenticateUser` upgraded to return permissions; 13 actions gated across 7 permission keys
- `src/app/api/admin/account-settings/route.ts` — `authenticate()` rewritten from boolean to `{ role, permissions }`; all 13 actions require `canManageAccounts`

**What could break:**
- Staff/manager users created in the DB with missing permission keys will now be denied actions they previously could access (UI already hid these, but API allowed them)
- Managers using env `MANAGER_PASSWORD` (no username) get `permissions: {}` — BUT the centralized check only denies when `role !== "admin" && !permissions[key]`. Managers with empty permissions object will be denied. If this is a problem, those managers need DB user accounts with proper permissions, or use the admin env password.
- `getSetting` is now admin-only — staff/managers can no longer read arbitrary settings (this is intentional, fixes H-2)

**How to verify:** `npm run build` passes. Test admin login with admin password (full access). Test a staff user — they should only access actions matching their permission keys.

**Rollback:** `git revert bbbf894`

